hi this is preshtalwalker can you figure  out this problem which is driving people  crazy  your job is to put numbers in each of  the four boxes to make all of the  equations true  give it a try and when you're ready keep  watching the video for the solution  this problem is actually a system of  linear equations  we're actually going to manipulate the  equations and prove there is no possible  solution for this problem  the first horizontal equation says that  blue minus red is equal to nine  the second vertical equation says red  plus green is equal to two  we can add up these two equations  to conclude that blue plus green is  equal to 11.  we can then look at the first vertical  equation to say blue plus yellow is  equal to 12  and we can look at the second horizontal  equation  to get negative yellow plus green is  equal to negative fourteen i've  multiplied the second equation by  negative one  this is so that we can cancel out the  yellow variable  and then we get the result blue plus  green is equal to negative two  now if you focus on the two results we  have we have something that's  contradictory in one case we have blue  plus green is equal to 11. in another  equation we found blue plus green is  equal to negative 2.  it's not possible for these both to be  true at the same time  therefore we've reached a contradiction  and therefore this is impossible and  there is no solution to this equation to  the system of equations  now you might ask yourself is it just  because we have the numbers 9 14 12 and  2  is it possible that this system of  equations could have another solution if  we put different numbers  so if the first equation was equal to b1  if the second horizontal equation was b2  the first vertical equation was b3 and  if the second vertical equation was b4  is it possible could we actually figure  out a solution  this is the type of problem that you  would deal with in linear algebra  the result would be a vector of four  variables b1 b2 b3 and b4 and these are  constants which are known  this is going to be the result of four  equations  four variables which is blue red yellow  and green we can represent the system of  equations by a linear operator which we  can write as the following matrix  if we multiply the matrix by the vector  of variables we end up with the results  so the first line of the matrix says  blue minus red is equal to b1  the second line of the matrix says  yellow minus green is equal to b2 the  third line says blue plus yellow is  equal to b3 and the fourth line says red  plus green is equal to b4  and that represents the four equations  that we have on the left hand side  now we can solve this system of  equations if we invert the matrix we'll  then get a unique solution by  multiplying  the vector of b1 to b4 by the inverted  matrix  however you can only invert a matrix if  its determinant is not zero  this matrix has a determinant that's  equal to zero so we cannot find a unique  solution for these four variables  because the matrix has a determinant  equal to zero there are two possible  things that can happen  one is you might have no solutions which  is what we had in this video  another thing you could have is you  might have a system of equations that's  underspecified  you would have infinitely many solutions  if you had the equations x plus y equals  2 and 2x plus y equals four you can see  that the second equation is two times  the first equation you don't get any new  information and therefore it's like  putting a line right on top of itself  there are infinitely many solutions  so no matter how you try  and solve this system of equations  you're either going to end up with no  solutions or infinitely many solutions  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on facebook google plus and  patreon you can catch me on social